From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:35:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: Refuse XDomain DMA paths once the
 XDomain is unplugged

tb_approve_xdomain_paths() looks up the destination and NHI ports
before it takes tb->lock. A service driver can still ask for paths
while the domain is being stopped: thunderbolt-net enables them from
its connected work, which a ThunderboltIP login queued just before the
control channel was stopped. By then tb_stop() may have removed the
routers and cleared tb->root_switch, so tb_switch_find_port() follows
a NULL pointer, and the XDomain's parent router is a removed switch.

Take tb->lock first and return -ENODEV when the XDomain is unplugged
or the root switch is gone. tb_disconnect_xdomain_paths() already
skips an unplugged XDomain the same way.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4a7c0cffef4578ae258b77f165adeb512a6bd365)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
index a4d439f239..19c1389c63 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
@@ -3161,12 +3161,22 @@ static int tb_approve_xdomain_paths(struct tb *tb, struct tb_xdomain *xd,
 	struct tb_switch *sw;
 	int ret;
 
+	mutex_lock(&tb->lock);
+
+	/*
+	 * A service driver can still ask for paths after the XDomain was
+	 * unplugged or while the domain is being stopped, when the router
+	 * may already be gone and tb->root_switch is NULL.
+	 */
+	if (xd->is_unplugged || !tb->root_switch) {
+		mutex_unlock(&tb->lock);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	sw = tb_to_switch(xd->dev.parent);
 	dst_port = tb_port_at(xd->route, sw);
 	nhi_port = tb_switch_find_port(tb->root_switch, TB_TYPE_NHI);
 
-	mutex_lock(&tb->lock);
-
 	/*
 	 * When tunneling DMA paths the link should not enter CL states
 	 * so disable them now.
